  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation AFD - GG Sustainable Infrastructure Projects Preparation Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;AFD Global Gateway Investment Preparation Facility is an essential instrument to facilitate the construction of a pipeline of projects to scale up the Global Gateway, even beyond the current MFF. The need to prepare quality, bankable projects is one of the key pre-requisites for increasing investments in infrastructure in emerging and developing countries. In Sub-Saharan Africa, slow deployment of strategic and sustainable infrastructures is not only due to the scarcity of financial resources, but also to the low availability of projects that are based on international standards and best practices. Emerging markets tend to rush into procurement without proper understanding of project costs and impacts. To address this challenge, adequate project preparation is key as it ensures alignment of public sector needs and private investors&#xbf; engagement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; The facility would cover the financing of: pre-feasibility and feasibility studies, preliminary and detailed design studies, preparation studies; assessments of climate risk, vulnerability, ecosystem services, nature-based solutions; identification of innovative finance, including green finance, e.g. payments for ecosystem services; elaboration of tendering documentation including for Operation &amp; Maintenance, that is crucial to attract and secure potential international private operators; transaction advisory, which aims at attracting private stakeholders in relevant projects when feasible; TA supporting governments, regulators, utilities and sectors&#xbf; ecosystems in the framework of project preparation and implementation.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
